<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Link on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/link/</link><description>Recent content in Link on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 10 Feb 2010 12:21:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/link/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Poster Printer</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/poster-printer/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Feb 2010 12:21:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/poster-printer/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 14 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 19 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2010/02/10/poster-printer/"&gt;Poster Printer&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/" class="f"&gt;gHacks technology news&lt;/a&gt; by Martin on 2/10/10&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;Easy Poster Printer is a free software program for the Windows operating system that enables a user to create a poster out of an image or photo that is loaded into the software. Veteran users might already know the concept that is applied to those images from services such as &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2006/11/30/create-huge-rasterized-images-from-pictures/"&gt;Rasterbator&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href="http://www.ghacks.net/2008/10/30/create-large-wall-posters/"&gt;Block Posters&lt;/a&gt; which we reviewed earlier.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Free Image Editors</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/free-image-editors/</link><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2009 07:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/free-image-editors/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 3 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/TRV/~3/iSKwMlXyapI/p1"&gt;Free Image Editors&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.trustedreviews.com/" class="f"&gt;TrustedReviews Site-wide Feed&lt;/a&gt; by Cliff Smith on 11/16/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;img src="http://www.trustedreviews.com/images/article/summary/12242.jpg" style="display:inline" /&gt; Good image editing software doesn't have to cost hundreds of pounds&lt;img src="http://feeds.feedburner.com/~r/TRV/~4/iSKwMlXyapI" height="1" width="1" /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Nibbo Search</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nibbo-search/</link><pubDate>Fri, 03 Jul 2009 10:30:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/nibbo-search/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="float: right; margin-left: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3683401401/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3629/3683401401_78207e5ee3_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style=" margin-top: 0px;font-size:0.9em;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3683401401/"&gt;Nibbo Search&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Been testing a new search engine &lt;a href="http://www.nibbo.com/"&gt;http://www.nibbo.com/&lt;/a&gt; so far I like it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Its really a nice front end on existing search engines so you can search a number of things at the same time.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Pixelmator 1.4 adds new paint engine</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pixelmator-14-adds-new-paint-engine/</link><pubDate>Thu, 26 Feb 2009 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/pixelmator-14-adds-new-paint-engine/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 8 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 10 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 10px; overflow: auto; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0pt 0pt;"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/2009/02/20/pixelmator-1-4-adds-new-paint-engine/"&gt;Pixelmator 1.4 adds new paint engine&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em;"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/" class="f"&gt;Download Squad&lt;/a&gt; by Jay Hathaway on 20/02/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;p&gt;Filed under: &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/design/" rel="tag"&gt;Design&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/photo/" rel="tag"&gt;Photo&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/macintosh/" rel="tag"&gt;Macintosh&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="http://www.downloadsquad.com/category/productivity/" rel="tag"&gt;Productivity&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Easy Steps to Rip a DVD to ISO in Ubuntu 8.10</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/easy-steps-to-rip-dvd-to-iso-in-ubuntu/</link><pubDate>Fri, 20 Feb 2009 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/easy-steps-to-rip-dvd-to-iso-in-ubuntu/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 11 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Need this when I make the Linux switch&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="padding: 4px; background-color: #c3d9ff;"&gt;&lt;h3 style="margin:0px 3px;font-family:sans-serif"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="font-family:sans-serif;overflow:auto;width:100%;margin: 0px 10px"&gt;&lt;h2 style="margin: 0.25em 0 0 0"&gt;&lt;div class=""&gt;&lt;a href="http://feedproxy.google.com/~r/SimplyJun/~3/G_vOtx3IlsY/easy-steps-to-rip-dvd-to-iso-in-ubuntu.html"&gt;Easy Steps to Rip a DVD to ISO in Ubuntu 8.10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/h2&gt; &lt;div style="margin-bottom: 0.5em"&gt;via &lt;a href="http://www.junauza.com/" class="f"&gt;TECH SOURCE FROM BOHOL&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="mailto:noreply@blogger.com"&gt;noreply@blogger.com&lt;/a&gt; (jun auza) on 2/19/09&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjxd5Wj5sG1z1YqwGE-zH8AzDPKxS3_3Ak223zEgjHp8c8N2KahxoGIbBWBqcy5sBhvGr2shu6I10zmLiF2L_hOQkAgmHbWLfMnXiA3vte4knwCVJeZaLA5UqAjWp-upu7SyINSXHDAUNI/s1600-h/dvd-burner.png"&gt;&lt;img style="margin:0pt 10px 10px 0pt;float:left;width:200px;height:200px" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjxd5Wj5sG1z1YqwGE-zH8AzDPKxS3_3Ak223zEgjHp8c8N2KahxoGIbBWBqcy5sBhvGr2shu6I10zmLiF2L_hOQkAgmHbWLfMnXiA3vte4knwCVJeZaLA5UqAjWp-upu7SyINSXHDAUNI/s320/dvd-burner.png" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;An ISO file is the easiest and most universal method for backing up a DVD. The file is an archive file specifically for DVD VIDEO_TS and AUDIO_TS files, and is an exact copy of the disc. ISO files can be quickly burned to a new dvd using standard burning software, making it the optimal choice for storing backups.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;In Windows, third-party software is the only way to backup a DVD. Luckily, Ubuntu Linux has removed this need, and as a result, you can backup your dvds using a standard feature built into the OS &amp;ndash;no software or Terminal required.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;This tutorial is written using Ubuntu 8.10 Intrepid Ibex. It will also work with 8.04.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 1:&lt;/span&gt; Insert the DVD you wish to backup into your optical drive and wait for the dvd icon to appear on your Desktop.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 2:&lt;/span&gt; Right-click on the DVD icon and choose &amp;lsquo;Copy Disc&amp;rsquo; from the menu.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 3:&lt;/span&gt; A dialog box will appear. In the drop-down box next to &amp;lsquo;Copy to&amp;hellip;&amp;rsquo;, choose FILE IMAGE.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjn8GTD_-opAqcDXdQgVc9RWZ9vY88p5EQ6QlTd133hesLuIYf_7LA_h-Fld3kvQb8gXbwQF4QOPPLZmphyyFYRgf-L1vBS64QWNifH3wSBBG52FnyECyb4TXilUsmJdXZdfW6MiR1Jb8w/s1600-h/Step+1_Choose+File+Image.png"&gt;&lt;img style="margin:0px auto 10px;display:block;text-align:center;width:379px;height:250px" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjn8GTD_-opAqcDXdQgVc9RWZ9vY88p5EQ6QlTd133hesLuIYf_7LA_h-Fld3kvQb8gXbwQF4QOPPLZmphyyFYRgf-L1vBS64QWNifH3wSBBG52FnyECyb4TXilUsmJdXZdfW6MiR1Jb8w/s400/Step+1_Choose+File+Image.png" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 4:&lt;/span&gt; Press the WRITE button.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 5:&lt;/span&gt; Choose a location to save the ISO.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgTdUC-rNC_NhA6eVBlIXMlljiF-Qpf4zCkIRXN0Hz1OiQQtudFUApOHl9EixXqBuQv-Zc0pjtx3yoqEGsl_sMwMkZb8LdGyAZWrw648_OYbgA0EeJpE3ileEwQvMS1cLyTFbCngirzKww/s1600-h/Step+2_Save+as.png"&gt;&lt;img style="margin:0px auto 10px;display:block;text-align:center;width:400px;height:327px" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgTdUC-rNC_NhA6eVBlIXMlljiF-Qpf4zCkIRXN0Hz1OiQQtudFUApOHl9EixXqBuQv-Zc0pjtx3yoqEGsl_sMwMkZb8LdGyAZWrw648_OYbgA0EeJpE3ileEwQvMS1cLyTFbCngirzKww/s400/Step+2_Save+as.png" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 6:&lt;/span&gt; Wait for the progress bar to reach the end. It will say &amp;lsquo;Successfully Copied&amp;rsquo;. Close the window and remove the DVD.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiSphq8ryMNfKHIw3uM2Ig6FRsb1YmtJAI2oPXvoKldZB3GWPGbfETqnIemHGxoJj-eXwsxxklH4Q6WsmUjYG0V8GlU4a7Lw_s8B3GJ1Ya5lKi3DYqbKoWueELZfXnCxnMwEwrTLo6tWc0/s1600-h/Step+3_Copying.png"&gt;&lt;img style="margin:0px auto 10px;display:block;text-align:center;width:377px;height:195px" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEiSphq8ryMNfKHIw3uM2Ig6FRsb1YmtJAI2oPXvoKldZB3GWPGbfETqnIemHGxoJj-eXwsxxklH4Q6WsmUjYG0V8GlU4a7Lw_s8B3GJ1Ya5lKi3DYqbKoWueELZfXnCxnMwEwrTLo6tWc0/s400/Step+3_Copying.png" alt="" border="0" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 7:&lt;/span&gt; You can test the ISO and confirm it works using VLC media player. If you don&amp;rsquo;t have VLC installed, you can install it via the Terminal and this code: sudo apt-get install vlc .&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 8:&lt;/span&gt; If you want to extract the VOB files from the ISO, right-click and choose &amp;rsquo;extract here&amp;rsquo;. It will take about ten minutes, but the video_ts and audio_ts folders will be extracted to the same location.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Step 9:&lt;/span&gt; If you want to convert the ISO into a smaller file, such as an XviD or x264, you can either extract the VOBs and use DVD::RIP, or download Handbrake and rip directly from the ISO&amp;ndash;both run smoothly on Ubuntu.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt; &lt;span style="font-style:italic"&gt;Fair Warning: In some countries, backing up DVDs you legally own is not legal&amp;ndash;for example, in the US, copying a commercial DVD violates the DCMA. Be sure to check with the laws in your country before proceeding.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;This tutorial was prepared for &amp;ldquo;Tech Source from Bohol&amp;rdquo; by &lt;span style="font-weight:bold"&gt;Blair Mathis&lt;/span&gt; of &lt;a href="http://laptoplogic.com/"&gt;LaptopLogic.com&lt;/a&gt;, your premier source for latest notebook reviews.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span class="Apple-style-span" style="color: rgb(0, 0, 238); text-decoration: underline;"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 1px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: #c3d9ff; font-size: 1px !important; line-height: 0px !important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>50 Free Photoshop Brush Sets You Should Bookmark</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/50-free-photoshop-brush-sets-you-should/</link><pubDate>Thu, 05 Feb 2009 12:19:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/50-free-photoshop-brush-sets-you-should/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 71 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 108 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="margin: 0px 2px; padding-top: 1px; background-color: rgb(195, 217, 255); font-size: 1px ! important; line-height: 0px ! important;"&gt; &lt;/div&gt; &lt;div style="margin: 0px 10px; overflow: auto; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;"&gt;&